<div class="top"><div class="wrap"><span>HISTORIC ARMY AIRCRAFT FLIGHT · MIDDLE WALLOP, HAMPSHIRE</span><span>KEEPING OUR AVIATION HERITAGE ALIVE</span></div></div><header class="nav"><div class="wrap navinner"><a class="brand" href="#home"><img alt="HAAF proposed new logo" class="brand-logo" src="images/logo.webp"/><div><strong>HAAF</strong><small>HISTORIC ARMY AIRCRAFT FLIGHT</small></div></a><nav class="links"><a href="#about">OUR STORY</a><a href="#aircraft">AIRCRAFT</a><a href="#galleries">PHOTO GALLERIES</a><a href="#visiting-aircraft">VISITING AIRCRAFT</a><a href="#visit">VISIT &amp; EVENTS</a><a href="#appearances">BOOK THE FLIGHT</a><a href="#stem">STEM &amp; EDUCATION</a><a href="#contact">CONTACT</a><a href="#support">SUPPORT HAAF</a><a href="#shop">SHOP</a><a class="btn" href="#support">SUPPORT THE FLIGHT</a><a href="#find-us">Find Us</a></nav></div></header><main><section class="hero" id="home"><svg aria-hidden="true" class="plane" viewbox="0 0 900 350"><path d="M75 185 L360 161 L450 85 L490 83 L478 160 L770 188 L810 209 L478 206 L470 265 L565 299 L559 315 L455 286 L351 315 L345 299 L441 265 L431 206 L90 210 Z" fill="#e7ece9"></path></svg><div class="wrap"><div class="eyebrow">PRESERVING THE PAST · INSPIRING THE FUTURE</div><h1>Keeping Army Aviation History Alive.</h1><p>Discover the aircraft, people and stories behind Britain's historic Army aviation heritage.</p><div class="actions"><a class="btn" href="#aircraft">EXPLORE OUR AIRCRAFT</a><a class="btn outline" href="#visit">PLAN YOUR VISIT</a></div></div></section><div class="ribbon"><div class="wrap"><div><strong>Help keep history flying.</strong> <span>Support preservation, engineering and the next generation of volunteers.</span></div><a href="#support" style="font-weight:bold;font-size:12px">SUPPORT THE FLIGHT →</a></div></div><section class="section" id="aircraft"><div class="wrap"><div class="heading"><div><div class="eyebrow">THE COLLECTION</div><h2>Meet the aircraft</h2></div><p>Explore the historic fixed-wing aircraft and helicopters that tell the story of British Army aviation.</p></div><div class="grid3"><article class="tile"><div class="art"><svg viewbox="0 0 500 230"><path d="M28 125 L202 111 L244 30 L268 30 L266 110 L456 126 L471 140 L268 138 L266 183 L323 209 L317 220 L251 197 L181 220 L176 209 L236 183 L233 138 L29 142 Z" fill="#d8e0de"></path></svg></div><div class="tilebody"><h3>DHC-2 Beaver</h3><p>Discover a remarkable utility aircraft and its role in Army aviation.</p><span class="arrow">DISCOVER THE AIRCRAFT →</span><a class="gallery-card-link" href="#gallery-1">VIEW PHOTOS &amp; AIRCRAFT PROFILE →</a></div></article><article class="tile"><div class="art green"><svg viewbox="0 0 500 230"><path d="M65 115h355v7H65zM238 62h7v98h-7zM180 122c15-38 90-39 109 0l20 28H161zM287 135l143 27-2 7-148-16zM174 155h145v7H174zM190 170h100v6H190zM192 183h100v5H192z" fill="#e0e6dd"></path></svg></div><div class="tilebody"><h3>Westland Scout</h3><p>Explore a classic British Army helicopter and its service heritage.</p><span class="arrow">DISCOVER THE AIRCRAFT →</span><a class="gallery-card-link" href="#gallery-2">VIEW PHOTOS &amp; AIRCRAFT PROFILE →</a></div></article><article class="tile"><div class="art sand"><svg viewbox="0 0 500 230"><path d="M40 127h410v6H40zM240 62h6v125h-6zM205 125c0-33 64-33 72 0l24 32H178zM277 148l128 20-3 7-131-16zM194 176h96v5h-96z" fill="#e5e9e6"></path></svg></div><div class="tilebody"><h3>Sioux AH.1</h3><p>Learn about one of the most recognisable helicopters of its generation.</p><span class="arrow">DISCOVER THE AIRCRAFT →</span><a class="gallery-card-link" href="#gallery-3">VIEW PHOTOS &amp; AIRCRAFT PROFILE →</a></div></article><article class="tile"><div class="art green"><img alt="Auster AOP.9 XR244 on the apron" src="images/auster-aop9.jpg" style="width:100%;height:100%;object-fit:cover"/></div><div class="tilebody"><h3>Auster AOP.9</h3><p>British Army air observation post aircraft. A dedicated profile can cover its operational role, engineering, restoration and HAAF history.</p><span class="arrow">FULL AIRCRAFT PROFILE · CONTENT TO FOLLOW</span><a class="gallery-card-link" href="#gallery-4">VIEW PHOTOS &amp; AIRCRAFT PROFILE →</a></div></article><article class="tile"><div class="art"><svg viewbox="0 0 500 230"><path d="M25 126 L190 118 L244 65 L260 65 L286 118 L475 126 L475 140 L282 137 L266 188 L328 209 L320 220 L250 200 L180 220 L174 209 L234 188 L222 137 L25 140 Z" fill="#d8e0de"></path></svg></div><div class="tilebody"><h3>de Havilland Chipmunk T.10</h3><p>A classic military training aircraft. Its profile can include technical specifications, photographs and the history of the aircraft associated with HAAF.</p><span class="arrow">FULL AIRCRAFT PROFILE · CONTENT TO FOLLOW</span><a class="gallery-card-link" href="#gallery-5">VIEW PHOTOS &amp; AIRCRAFT PROFILE →</a></div></article><article class="tile"><div class="art sand"><svg aria-hidden="true" viewbox="0 0 500 230"><path d="M18 122 L202 113 L239 52 L259 52 L279 113 L482 122 L482 139 L277 136 L263 181 L320 208 L316 217 L250 198 L184 217 L180 208 L237 181 L223 136 L18 139 Z" fill="#e5e9e6"></path></svg></div><div class="tilebody"><h3>Taylorcraft (Auster) Mk.1</h3><p>Historic Army observation aircraft. Photographs, history and technical details to be added by the HAAF team.</p><span class="arrow">FULL AIRCRAFT PROFILE · CONTENT TO FOLLOW</span><a class="gallery-card-link" href="#gallery-6">VIEW PHOTOS &amp; AIRCRAFT PROFILE →</a></div></article><article class="tile"><div class="art"><img alt="Skeeter — Static Display" src="images/skeeter.jpg" style="width:100%;height:100%;object-fit:cover"/></div><div class="tilebody"><h3>Skeeter — Static Display</h3><p>Non-flying tow-in exhibit for community and veterans’ events.</p><a class="gallery-card-link" href="#appearances">ENQUIRE ABOUT A STATIC DISPLAY →</a></div></article><article class="tile"><div class="art"><img alt="Gazelle — Static Display" src="images/gazelle.jpg" style="width:100%;height:100%;object-fit:cover"/></div><div class="tilebody"><h3>Gazelle — Static Display</h3><p>Non-flying tow-in exhibit for remembrance and public events.</p><a class="gallery-card-link" href="#appearances">ENQUIRE ABOUT A STATIC DISPLAY →</a></div></article></div><div style="margin-top:36px;padding:25px;background:#e6e3d9"><h3 style="font:normal 26px Georgia,serif;margin:0 0 10px">Additional aircraft and archive material</h3><p style="line-height:1.7">Space for further aircraft, restoration projects and historic collection records, subject to confirmation by the HAAF team.</p></div></div></section><section class="section" id="galleries"><div class="wrap"><div class="heading"><div><div class="eyebrow">AIRCRAFT PHOTOGRAPHY</div><h2>Aircraft photo galleries</h2></div><p>Explore each aircraft through cockpit, exterior, flying, archive and engineering photographs. Select a photograph to view it larger.</p></div><div aria-label="Choose an aircraft gallery" class="gallery-tabs"><button class="gallery-tab selected" data-gallery="1" type="button">DHC-2 Beaver</button><button class="gallery-tab" data-gallery="2" type="button">Westland Scout</button><button class="gallery-tab" data-gallery="3" type="button">Sioux AH.1</button><button class="gallery-tab" data-gallery="4" type="button">Auster AOP.9</button><button class="gallery-tab" data-gallery="5" type="button">de Havilland Chipmunk T.10</button><button class="gallery-tab" data-gallery="6" type="button">Taylorcraft (Auster) Mk.1</button></div><div id="gallery-panels"><div class="gallery-panel active" id="gallery-1"><h3>DHC-2 Beaver — photo gallery</h3><div class="gallery-grid"><div class="gallery-photo"><button aria-label="Enlarge Beaver cockpit photograph" class="gallery-open" type="button"><img alt="Black-and-white photograph of a de Havilland cockpit in a hangar, looking forward across the dual controls and instrument panels" src="images/cockpit-hangar.jpg"/></button><div class="gallery-caption">Cockpit &amp; flight deck 